| `scripts/check_python_version.py` | The shared interpreter-floor guard fails early, with a plain message, when the interpreter is older than `requires-python`; reads the requirement with a parser the old interpreter can run. | `make check-python`; imported by preflight | [`PY`](settings.md#make-variables) | Assumes a 3.10 floor when `pyproject.toml` declares none. Judges the major/minor floor, not installed packages; check-venv judges those. | [limits-and-troubleshooting.md](../guides/limits-and-troubleshooting.md), [dev-loops.md](../guides/dev-loops.md) | always |
